{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Local code-review preview remediation: removed the tautological mock calibration unit test because it only rechecked metric arithmetic and did not exercise T10 semantics. Added a RED-first contract test requiring the standing eval to gate pass cases with no_fire_on_good_cases and finding cases with recall_on_seeded_defects. Initial wiring also exposed that emits_valid_findings validates a later-stage schema requiring severity, while criterion-finder outputs are intentionally pre-severity; that mismatched scorer made every real finding fail for the wrong reason, so the final T10 spec gates on the two applicable semantic scorers only. Offline spec validation reports both scorers as gating. Focused tests: 35 passed; lint PASS; typecheck PASS. The real standing eval then ran all ten cases for three epochs with coverage=1.0, epoch_pass=[true,true,true], gate=at_least(2), passed=true. The previously recorded criteria-eval result remains recall=1.0, false_accept=0.0, and full stability."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786558912717071001,"uuid":"9608d900-47d7-4277-8af7-3a48fad0ff7c"}